---Encapsulates settings for enabling QueryInsights on an ExecuteScheduledQueryRequest.
---@class aws.timestream_query.ScheduledQueryInsights
---@field Mode aws.timestream_query.ScheduledQueryInsightsMode|string Provides the following modes to enable ScheduledQueryInsights:

---@alias aws.timestream_query.ScheduledQueryInsightsMode "ENABLED_WITH_RATE_CONTROL"|"DISABLED"

---Provides various insights and metrics related to the ExecuteScheduledQueryRequest that was executed.
---@class aws.timestream_query.ScheduledQueryInsightsResponse
---@field QuerySpatialCoverage? aws.timestream_query.QuerySpatialCoverage Provides insights into the spatial coverage of the query, including the table with sub-optimal (max) spatial pruning. This information can help you identify areas for improvement in your partitioning strategy to enhance spatial pruning.
---@field QueryTemporalRange? aws.timestream_query.QueryTemporalRange Provides insights into the temporal range of the query, including the table with the largest (max) time range. Following are some of the potential options for optimizing time-based pruning:
---@field QueryTableCount aws.timestream_query.Long Indicates the number of tables in the query.
---@field OutputRows aws.timestream_query.Long Indicates the total number of rows returned as part of the query result set. You can use this data to validate if the number of rows in the result set have changed as part of the query tuning exercise.
---@field OutputBytes aws.timestream_query.Long Indicates the size of query result set in bytes. You can use this data to validate if the result set has changed as part of the query tuning exercise.

---@alias aws.timestream_query.ScheduledQueryList aws.timestream_query.ScheduledQuery[]

---@alias aws.timestream_query.ScheduledQueryName string

---@alias aws.timestream_query.ScheduledQueryRunStatus "AUTO_TRIGGER_SUCCESS"|"AUTO_TRIGGER_FAILURE"|"MANUAL_TRIGGER_SUCCESS"|"MANUAL_TRIGGER_FAILURE"

---Run summary for the scheduled query
---@class aws.timestream_query.ScheduledQueryRunSummary
---@field InvocationTime? aws.timestream_query.Time InvocationTime for this run. This is the time at which the query is scheduled to run. Parameter @scheduled_runtime can be used in the query to get the value.
---@field TriggerTime? aws.timestream_query.Time The actual time when the query was run.
---@field RunStatus? aws.timestream_query.ScheduledQueryRunStatus The status of a scheduled query run.
---@field ExecutionStats? aws.timestream_query.ExecutionStats Runtime statistics for a scheduled run.
---@field QueryInsightsResponse? aws.timestream_query.ScheduledQueryInsightsResponse Provides various insights and metrics related to the run summary of the scheduled query.
---@field ErrorReportLocation? aws.timestream_query.ErrorReportLocation S3 location for error report.
---@field FailureReason? aws.timestream_query.ErrorMessage Error message for the scheduled query in case of failure. You might have to look at the error report to get more detailed error reasons.

---@alias aws.timestream_query.ScheduledQueryRunSummaryList aws.timestream_query.ScheduledQueryRunSummary[]

---@alias aws.timestream_query.ScheduledQueryState "ENABLED"|"DISABLED"

